# Input Validation Patterns - Quick Reference

## Common Validation Patterns

### Email Validation
```javascript
body('email')
  .trim()
  .normalizeEmail()                    // Removes dots, capitalization, etc.
  .isEmail()                           // Validates email format
  .withMessage('Invalid email address')
  .isLength({ max: 255 })              // Prevent DoS via long emails
  .withMessage('Email too long')
```

### Username Validation
```javascript
body('username')
  .trim()
  .escape()                            // Prevents XSS
  .isLength({ min: 3, max: 30 })
  .withMessage('Username must be 3-30 characters')
  .matches(/^[a-zA-Z0-9_-]+$/)         // Alphanumeric, underscore, hyphen only
  .withMessage('Username can only contain letters, numbers, underscores, and hyphens')
```

### Password Validation (Before Hashing)
```javascript
body('password')
  .isLength({ min: 12, max: 128 })
  .withMessage('Password must be 12-128 characters')
  .matches(/[a-z]/)                    // At least one lowercase
  .withMessage('Password must contain at least one lowercase letter')
  .matches(/[A-Z]/)                    // At least one uppercase
  .withMessage('Password must contain at least one uppercase letter')
  .matches(/[0-9]/)                    // At least one number
  .withMessage('Password must contain at least one number')
  .matches(/[^a-zA-Z0-9]/)             // At least one special char
  .withMessage('Password must contain at least one special character')
```

### Numeric ID Validation
```javascript
param('id')
  .isInt({ min: 1, max: 2147483647 })  // Positive integer within range
  .withMessage('ID must be a positive integer')
  .toInt()                             // Convert to integer safely
```

### Pagination Parameters
```javascript
// For query parameters
query('page')
  .optional()
  .isInt({ min: 1 })
  .withMessage('Page must be at least 1')
  .toInt(),
query('limit')
  .optional()
  .isInt({ min: 1, max: 100 })         // Never allow more than 100
  .withMessage('Limit must be between 1 and 100')
  .toInt(),
query('sort')
  .optional()
  .isIn(['id', 'name', 'created_at']) // Whitelist allowed fields
  .withMessage('Invalid sort field')
```

### Search/Filter Validation
```javascript
query('search')
  .optional()
  .trim()
  .escape()                           // Escape HTML entities
  .isLength({ max: 100 })
  .withMessage('Search term too long'),
query('date_from')
  .optional()
  .isISO8601()
  .withMessage('Invalid date format'),
query('status')
  .optional()
  .isIn(['active', 'inactive', 'pending'])
  .withMessage('Invalid status value')
```

### URL Validation
```javascript
body('website')
  .optional()
  .isURL({
    protocols: ['http', 'https'],
    require_tld: true,
    require_protocol: true
  })
  .withMessage('Invalid URL format')
```

### Phone Number Validation
```javascript
body('phone')
  .optional()
  .trim()
  .matches(/^\+?[1-9]\d{1,14}$/)       // E.164 format
  .withMessage('Invalid phone number format (E.164)')
```

### Enum/Select Validation
```javascript
body('role')
  .isIn(['user', 'admin', 'moderator'])
  .withMessage('Invalid role'),
body('priority')
  .isIn(['low', 'medium', 'high', 'urgent'])
  .withMessage('Invalid priority value')
```

### JSON Field Validation
```javascript
body('metadata')
  .optional()
  .custom(value => {
    try {
      if (typeof value === 'string') {
        JSON.parse(value);
      }
      return true;
    } catch {
      throw new Error('Invalid JSON format');
    }
  })
  .isObject()
  .withMessage('Metadata must be a JSON object')
```

---

## Common Express Validations

### Required vs Optional Fields
```javascript
// Required field
body('name')
  .notEmpty()
  .withMessage('Name is required')
  .trim()
  .isLength({ max: 100 })

// Optional field
body('middle_name')
  .optional()
  .trim()
  .isLength({ max: 50 })
```

### String Sanitization Chain
```javascript
body('input')
  .trim()              // Remove whitespace from start/end
  .escape()            // Escape HTML entities (&, <, >, ", ')
  .blacklist('<>(){}') // Remove dangerous characters
  .normalizeEmail()    // For emails only
```

### Array Validation
```javascript
body('tags')
  .optional()
  .isArray({ max: 10 })
  .withMessage('Cannot have more than 10 tags')
  .custom(arr => arr.every(tag => 
    /^[a-z0-9-]+$/.test(tag)
  ))
  .withMessage('Tags must be lowercase alphanumeric with hyphens')
```

### File Upload Validation
```javascript
const upload = multer({
  limits: {
    fileSize: 5 * 1024 * 1024, // 5MB
    files: 3                   // Max 3 files
  },
  fileFilter: (req, file, cb) => {
    const allowedTypes = ['image/jpeg', 'image/png', 'image/gif'];
    if (allowedTypes.includes(file.mimetype)) {
      cb(null, true);
    } else {
      cb(new Error('Invalid file type. Only JPEG, PNG, and GIF allowed.'));
    }
  }
});
```

---

## Custom Validators

### Check for SQL Injection Patterns
```javascript
const containsSqlInjection = (value) => {
  const patterns = [
    /(\b(SELECT|INSERT|UPDATE|DELETE|DROP|UNION|EXEC|ALTER)\b)/i,
    /(--)|(\/\*)|(\*\/)/,
    /;.*\b(WAITFOR|DELAY)\b/i
  ];
  return patterns.some(pattern => pattern.test(value));
};

body('query')
  .custom(value => {
    if (containsSqlInjection(value)) {
      throw new Error('Invalid input detected');
    }
    return true;
  })
```

### Check for XSS Patterns
```javascript
body('content')
  .custom(value => {
    const xssPatterns = [
      /<script\b[^<]*(?:(?!<\/script>)<[^<]*)*<\/script>/gi,
      /javascript:/gi,
      /on\w+\s*=/gi
    ];
    if (xssPatterns.some(pattern => pattern.test(value))) {
      throw new Error('Potentially dangerous content detected');
    }
    return true;
  })
```

### UUID Validation
```javascript
const { isUUID } = require('validator');

param('id')
  .custom(value => {
    if (!isUUID(value, 4)) { // UUID v4
      throw new Error('Invalid UUID format');
    }
    return true;
  })
```

---

## Response Validation (Sanitize Output)

### Remove Sensitive Fields
```javascript
const sanitizeUser = (user) => {
  const { password, passwordHash, refreshToken, ...safeUser } = user;
  return safeUser;
};

res.json({ user: sanitizeUser(user) });
```

### Limit Response Data
```javascript
const allowedUserFields = ['id', 'name', 'email'];

res.json({
  user: allowedUserFields.reduce((obj, key) => {
    obj[key] = user[key];
    return obj;
  }, {})
});
```

---

## Middleware Patterns

### Validation Middleware
```javascript
const validate = (validations) => async (req, res, next) => {
  await Promise.all(validations.map(validation => validation.run(req)));

  const errors = validationResult(req);
  if (errors.isEmpty()) {
    return next();
  }

  res.status(400).json({
    error: 'Validation failed',
    details: errors.array()
  });
};

// Usage
router.post('/users', 
  validate([
    body('name').notEmpty(),
    body('email').isEmail()
  ]),
  handler
);
```

### Schema Validation with Joi (Alternative)
```javascript
const Joi = require('joi');

const userSchema = Joi.object({
  name: Joi.string().min(3).max(100).required(),
  email: Joi.string().email().required(),
  age: Joi.number().integer().min(0).max(150).optional()
});

router.post('/users', (req, res, next) => {
  const { error, value } = userSchema.validate(req.body, {
    abortEarly: false,
    stripUnknown: true
  });

  if (error) {
    return res.status(400).json({
      error: 'Validation failed',
      details: error.details.map(d => d.message)
    });
  }

  req.body = value; // Use sanitized values
  next();
});
```

---

## Security Checklist for Each Input

| Input Type | Validation Required | Sanitization Required |
|------------|-------------------|----------------------|
| Query Params | Type, range, format | Escape, trim |
| Path Params | Type, range | Parse to correct type |
| Body JSON | Schema, field constraints | Escape strings, serialize objects |
| Form Data | All of above | All of above |
| File Upload | Size, type, content | Scan for malware |
| Headers | Length, format | Don't trust headers blindly |

---

## Common Mistakes to Avoid

❌ **Don't do this:**
```javascript
// No validation
const id = req.params.id;
db.query(`SELECT * FROM users WHERE id = ${id}`);

// Only client-side validation
// Can be bypassed easily
```

✅ **Do this instead:**
```javascript
// Server-side validation
const { id } = await param('id').isInt().run(req);
db.query('SELECT * FROM users WHERE id = $1', [id.value]);
```

❌ **Don't use regex only for validation:**
```javascript
// Only checks format, not length or dangerous content
.matches(/^[a-z]+$/)
```

✅ **Combine multiple validations:**
```javascript
.trim()
.escape()
.isLength({ min: 1, max: 100 })
.matches(/^[a-zA-Z0-9_-]+$/)
```

