## Security Vulnerabilities Fixed

### 1. Path Traversal
**Before:** 
```javascript
app.get('/users/:id', (req, res) => {
  // No validation - vulnerable to ../../etc/passwd
});
```

**After:**
```javascript
const isValidUserId = (id) => {
  const numId = parseInt(id, 10);
  return !isNaN(numId) && numId > 0 && numId <= Number.MAX_SAFE_INTEGER;
};

app.get('/users/:id', validateRequest((req) => {
  if (!isValidUserId(req.params.id)) {
    return { error: { message: 'Invalid user ID' } };
  }
  return { error: null };
}), /* ... */);
```

---

### 2. XSS Attacks
**Before:**
```javascript
// Directly returns user input - vulnerable
res.json({ name: req.body.name });
```

**After:**
```javascript
const sanitizeUser = (user) => ({
  name: typeof user.name === 'string' 
    ? xss(user.name.trim()).substring(0, 100) 
    : null
});
res.json({ data: sanitizeUser(user) });
```

---

### 3. DoS via Large Payloads
**Before:**
```javascript
// No limit - can accept unlimited payload size
app.use(express.json());
```

**After:**
```javascript
// Strict 10kb limit
app.use(express.json({ 
  limit: '10kb',
  strict: true
}));
```

---

### 4. Information Disclosure
**Before:**
```javascript
// No error handling - stack traces exposed
app.get('/users', async (req, res) => {
  const users = await db.query('SELECT * FROM users'); // Could fail
  res.json(users);
});
```

**After:**
```javascript
// Proper error handling
app.get('/users', asyncHandler(async (req, res) => {
  try {
    const users = await db.query('SELECT * FROM users');
    res.json({ data: users });
  } catch (error) {
    throw new AppError('Failed to fetch users', 500);
  }
}));

// Global handler only shows details in development
app.use((err, req, res, next) => {
  const isDevelopment = NODE_ENV === 'development';
  res.status(err.statusCode || 500).json({
    error: {
      message: isDevelopment ? err.message : 'An error occurred',
      ...(isDevelopment && { stack: err.stack })
    }
  });
});
```

---

### 5. Missing Security Headers
**Before:**
```javascript
// No security headers at all
```

**After:**
```javascript
app.use(helmet({
  contentSecurityPolicy: {
    directives: {
      defaultSrc: ["'self'"],
      scriptSrc: ["'self'"],
    },
  },
  hsts: {
    maxAge: 31536000,
    includeSubDomains: true,
    preload: true
  },
